menu "Lua"
    config LUA_MAXSTACK
        int "Maximum Lua stack size (slots)"
        range 1000 1073741823
        default 1000000
        help
            Maximum number of Lua stack slots a lua_State may grow to.
            The unit is slots (Lua values), not bytes. Each slot holds
            one value and occupies about 8 bytes on 32-bit ESP targets.

            This is a growth cap, not a reservation. The stack starts
            small and expands on demand until it hits this limit.

            Size this cap together with the calling FreeRTOS task
            stack. Raising it does not grow the C stack: a 2 KB task
            stack will overflow long before a large Lua stack is
            usable.

    config LUA_USE_PSRAM
        bool "Prefer PSRAM for large Lua allocations"
        depends on SPIRAM
        default n
        help
            Route luaL_newstate() through a heap_caps allocator so large
            objects can live in PSRAM. A custom allocator passed to
            lua_newstate() is left unchanged.

            Allocations of 4 KiB or more (growing table arrays, long
            strings, a large Lua stack) prefer PSRAM. Smaller objects
            stay in internal RAM: the interpreter walks them randomly,
            which is slower in PSRAM. Either region is a fallback if
            the preferred heap cannot satisfy the request.
endmenu
